factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The reel_script and caption say the mud lamps are made 'by machine motor' (மின் மோட்டார் மூலம்) for both the five-faced and small lamps, which matches the article; however the reel_script's line about 'முந்நூறு ரூபாய்' and prices are consistent — no issue there. Problem found: the article says 'பெரிய விளக்கு, 300 ரூபாய்' and 'ஐந்து முகம் கொண்ட விளக்கு ஒன்று, 15 ரூபாய்' — consistent. Real problem: the article says the five-faced and single-faced lamps and small lamps are made by machine, but the draft's slides_spec and reel_script omit that the article says these lamps are used daily in temples (கோவில்களில் நாள்தோறும் பயன்படுத்தப்படும்) — minor omission, see next item.
  The reel_script states the festival is on the 24th without the month, which is acceptable only if it matches; the article says 'வரும், 24ல்' so the date is consistent.
  The reel_script says 'மண்பாண்டத் தொழிலாளர்கள் விளக்குகளைத் தயாரிக்கும் பணியில் ஈடுபட்டுள்ளனர்' — consistent with the article.
  The caption says the lamps are made 'வழக்கமாக ஒரு மாதத்துக்கு முன்பே' which is consistent with the article.
  The caption claims the making of mud lamps requires drying in sun and baking in a kiln, but the slides_spec line says 'சுடாவிட்டால் விளக்கு தரமாக இருக்காது' — consistent with the article's claim that otherwise the lamp will not be of good quality.
  The reel_script omits the important fact that the lamps are sold to wholesale traders and that the article quotes lamp makers; this is minor and not a required fact.
