  The caption says the man was arrested 'அவர் கேட்காததால்' (because he did not listen) as the direct cause, which combines the warning with the arrest in a way the article does not state explicitly; the article says he remained after being warned, then was arrested, which is roughly consistent but the caption frames the arrest as caused by non-compliance with the warning.
  The reel_script's 'போலீசார் வழக்குப் பதிவு செய்து' and 'போலீசாரால் கைது' are consistent, but the caption's 'இடையூறு செய்தவர் கைது' headline and the slide title 'போலீசார் வழக்குப் பதிவு' are fine; however the caption's English line 'man arrested for disturbing public' is an added claim not in the article's content beyond disturbance, which is acceptable.
  The reel_script states the man was 'கைது செய்யப்பட்டார்' while the article says 'கைது செய்தனர்' and 'வழக்கு பதிவு செய்து விசாரணை நடத்தி வருகின்றனர' — consistent, but the reel_script omits the article's explicit note that the man was standing in the middle of the road and causing disruption to traffic in the first sentence; this is covered.
